{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Xcode asks to “Trust & Enable” a macro","anchor":"Xcode-asks-to-Trust--Enable-a-macro"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" are compiler plugins, so the first build in Xcode"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prompts once per machine to trust the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxMacros"},{"type":"text","text":" target. Approve it in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"build error’s fix-it or under "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Settings → Packages"}]},{"type":"text","text":". On CI, pass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-skipMacroValidation"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — there’s no one to click the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dialog."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The first build is slow","type":"heading","anchor":"The-first-build-is-slow","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux depends on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift-syntax"},{"type":"text","text":", which the macro system compiles from source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on first build (a few minutes on CI-class hardware). It’s cached afterwards;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing is wrong. CI pipelines benefit from caching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".build\/"},{"type":"text","text":" or DerivedData."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Console shows “Re-entrant Store.send(…) — deferring”","type":"heading","anchor":"Console-shows-Re-entrant-Storesend-deferring","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Something called ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" synchronously from inside a reducer or plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hook — usually a plugin observing state and dispatching in ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setter fired during view updates. The store defers the inner action","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and runs it as a full cycle right after the current one, so state stays","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consistent — but the fault log is telling you the design wants that follow-up","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dispatched from an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`call to main actor-isolated initializer … in a synchronous nonisolated context`","type":"heading","anchor":"call-to-main-actor-isolated-initializer--in-a-synchronous-nonisolated-context","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The module is compiling in Swift 5 language mode with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SWIFT_DEFAULT_ACTOR_ISOLATION = MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux nonisolated struct","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only gets a nonisolated synthesized memberwise initializer under ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift 6"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mode"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"SWIFT_VERSION = 6.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); under Swift 5 mode the macro’s state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconstruction can’t call it, and adding an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"nonisolated init","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not rescue it. Switch the target to Swift 6 mode.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Error: “stored properties need an explicit type annotation”","type":"heading","anchor":"Error-stored-properties-need-an-explicit-type-annotation","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"var flag = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the compiler an inferred type, but macros can’t see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it — before this diagnostic existed, such a property was silently skipped and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its value reset on every dispatch. Write ","type":"text"},{"code":"var flag: Bool = false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies to combined declarations: split ","type":"text"},{"code":"var a, b: Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" into separate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declarations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Keychain writes fail with OSStatus −34018 (`errSecMissingEntitlement`)","type":"heading","anchor":"Keychain-writes-fail-with-OSStatus-%E2%88%9234018-errSecMissingEntitlement","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An unsigned local or CI build is using ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore"},{"text":" without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provisioning profile. This is a signing condition, not a prompt or a bug — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data-protection keychain never prompts.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is persisted, but nothing crashes either: the write logs, returns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the app continues. Ship provisioning-profile-signed builds with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessGroup: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to get real persistence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Adding a team-prefixed ","type":"text"},{"code":"keychain-access-groups","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement also works, and is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right call when you want the access group — but weigh it first, because it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes the app require a provisioning profile for every signed build. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a fix for a test host: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO"},{"type":"text","text":" embeds no entitlements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at all, so there is nothing for the entitlement to attach to. Let the write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degrade there. Details in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"`Test crashed with signal trap before establishing connection`","type":"heading","anchor":"Test-crashed-with-signal-trap-before-establishing-connection","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xcodebuild test"},{"text":" dies before any test runs, naming nothing useful. If the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"mints a device identity or writes a token at launch, suspect the Keychain: the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test host is unsigned, the write fails, and a trap takes the process down before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the test bundle can attach.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Current versions degrade instead of trapping here, so upgrading Swidux is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fix. To confirm the diagnosis on an older one, run the same scheme with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=YES"},{"text":" — if it gets past launch, the Keychain was the cause.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Edits disappear after a sync tick or an async load","type":"heading","anchor":"Edits-disappear-after-a-sync-tick-or-an-async-load","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Symptom: a keystroke, a toggle, or a whole entity vanishes — intermittently,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"usually while something is loading or syncing, and never reproducibly.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The cause is almost always a hand-rolled bridge from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"text":" work into the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps state in an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" observer tree and converts to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value-type snapshot on the way in and out (“pack” and “unpack”). If you pack a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"snapshot, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" something, and then unpack it, everything dispatched during"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" is silently overwritten:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var snapshot = AppState(observer: store.observer)   \/\/ ← packed BEFORE the await","await loadEverything(into: &snapshot)               \/\/ ← dispatches land here…","AppState.apply(snapshot, to: store.observer)        \/\/ ← …and are discarded here"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":" across a suspension point is the tell. The window is only as wide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":", which is why it presents as a rare glitch rather than a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reproducible bug.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" instead. It runs the async work with no","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access to state, then packs a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"fresh","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" snapshot, merges, and unpacks in a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step with no suspension point in between — so no dispatch can interleave:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["await store.mutate {","    try await api.fetchItems()          \/\/ no state in scope; nothing to stale","} merging: { items, state in","    state.items.merge(from: EntityStore(items)) { _, _ in false }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The persistence stack’s own async entry points already work this way — use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistence.rehydrate(into: store)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sync.setSyncEnabled(_:into: store)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a snapshot you manage yourself. ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hydrate(into: &state)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the exception,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and safe: it runs at launch, before the store exists.)"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Contributors-the-lint-plugin-doesnt-run--dev-tooling-is-missing","text":"Contributors: the lint plugin doesn’t run \/ dev tooling is missing","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dev tooling (the Persnoop linter, the DocC plugin) is gated behind a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gitignored "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dev-tooling"},{"type":"text","text":" sentinel file so it never leaks into consumers’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dependency graphs. Create it at the package root — and if the package was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already built without it, run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift package purge-cache"},{"type":"text","text":" so SwiftPM re-reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the manifest. See the repository’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CONTRIBUTING.md"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"A-Persisted-app-crashes-only-in-Release","text":"A `@Persisted` app crashes only in Release","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the crash is in fetching, make sure you’re on ≥ 1.3.0: generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Predicate"},{"type":"text","text":" over a protocol-required keypath traps under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-O"},{"type":"text","text":", which is why"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the macro generates a per-model "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiduxBatchFetchDescriptor"},{"type":"text","text":" — one for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"type":"text","text":" — and why every by-identifier read goes through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one instead of building a predicate inline. Run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift test -c release"},{"type":"text","text":" in CI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to catch this class of issue — Debug builds and default "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift test"},{"type":"text","text":" pass."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"],"anchor":"Reference"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Troubleshooting","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/mutate(awaiting:merging:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs async work that must not hold state across its suspensions, then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"folds the result into a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"freshly packed"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshot in one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"suspension-free step."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mutate"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"awaiting"},{"kind":"text","text":": () "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"merging"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/mutate(awaiting:merging:)","title":"mutate(awaiting:merging:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeychainKeyValueStore":{"type":"topic","title":"KeychainKeyValueStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyValueStore"},{"type":"text","text":" backed by the system Keychain."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"KeychainKeyValueStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeychainKeyValueStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeychainKeyValueStore","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keychainkeyvaluestore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxParentalGate"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxKillswitch"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","title":"KeyValueStore","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","title":"Macros"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","title":"EntityStore"}}}